  "effect": {
    "worthwhile_speedup": 1.1,
    "rationale": "Ten percent of a receiver's steady-state decode budget on one worker, the gain the single-worker before-after family requires of the lane route. A repeatable gain that size from the envelope's calibrated selectors frees frame time a receiver spends on more frames or more iterations; below it, routing waves by a calibrated envelope would not repay maintaining the calibration and its owner envelope. It lies strictly above one plus the pilot-derived resolution.",
