    },
    "equivalence_margin": 1.05,
    "equivalence_rationale": "Within five percent on a small-batch, incomplete-wave or native-build call, the envelope's routing costs a latency-bound or native-build consumer less than it would act on against the full-wave gain the family requires; a larger loss is a regression that consumer pays on every such call. The margin lies strictly above one plus the pilot-derived resolution, and a regression inside it is unresolved by this family and is not shown absent.",
